From 4f6dd0adf282cd070a66f9a9ba9ee79021944185 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:27:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! net: reconcile recently admitted transactions with
 peers continuously

Adapt relay epoch window selection to GetScopedTransactions vector-return API. The earlier immutable-snapshot owner removed output parameters; the relay-context insertion still writes nonexistent out_txs/out_root and returns void, which the actual normal native ChronikON/walletON compile rejects. Return the normalized epoch window directly, as cached and fallback branches already return vectors. Existing summary/diff callers compute the scoped commitment from that vector, preserving epoch selection, root policy, unknown-context fallback and salts.
---
 src/net/v2_protocol_handler.cpp | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/net/v2_protocol_handler.cpp b/src/net/v2_protocol_handler.cpp
index 4579aef4a0..dba027c1bf 100644
--- a/src/net/v2_protocol_handler.cpp
+++ b/src/net/v2_protocol_handler.cpp
@@ -766,10 +766,7 @@ std::vector<CTransactionRef> V2PeerProtocolHandler::GetScopedTransactions(
         // A relay epoch: the transactions admitted within the
         // reconciliation window, not the whole mempool.
         if (auto window{m_relay_epochs->RelayReconSet(context_id)}) {
-            out_txs = NormalizeCtorTxList(*window);
-            const lotus::v2::Hash root = ComputeSubtreeAHash(out_txs);
-            std::memcpy(out_root.begin(), root.data(), 32);
-            return;
+            return NormalizeCtorTxList(*window);
         }
     }
     if (scope == ReconScope::LIVE_MEMPOOL) {
